{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"A redundant stored row cannot be removed through the catalog command, so its startup warning continues even though the built-in remains active."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A future built-in that collides with an existing runtime entry could prevent startup, although that collision policy already existed before this change."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later owner decision may require updating the hard-coded test expectations, with no demonstrated runtime effect."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Filtering Haiku 5.5 from the frozen snapshot leaves its widened routing behavior outside that test, although widening itself follows the existing routing rules."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persisted operator route using an effort supported by the old runtime definition but not the new built-in causes the daemon to fail at startup."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The displayed pin reason omits earlier rationale, which remains available in the referenced evidence document."}]}